    {
      "what": "self-heating",
      "why": "Resistance follows world temperature only. The sheet's 7 mW/K dissipation factor is not modelled; above the 5 mW zero-power condition (max 1 % of the 500 mW max at 55 C), self-heating moves the real reading off the R/T table, so rating.power warns past 5 mW as beyond the load the sheet characterizes.",
