      "what": "power derating curve",
      "why": "The 5 mW threshold is the sheet's zero-power condition for the -40 to 125 C R/T table, not a damage limit. Vishay 29049 p1 gives 500 mW maximum power at 55 C (p2 derates from 100 % across 0 to 55 C to 0 % at -40 C and 85 C), so loads above 5 mW keep running and warn that unmodelled self-heating moves the real reading off the table.",
